From cf7fb6e3c47d688db76422117fc1b0151f2726c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Jacob <159104807+Justin24506@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:57:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] avcodec/jpeg2000dec: decode the tier-1 passes over
 packed flag columns

Replace the per-coefficient flag words with one 32-bit word per
four-row stripe column: the 3x6 significance neighbourhood in bits
0-17, then the per-row sign, refinement and visited marks and the two
stripe-edge signs. A new significant coefficient updates three words
instead of nine, and a context is a shift, a mask and one table load.
The visited marks also let the significance and refinement passes skip
whole columns without reading them.

The cleanup pass skips a run of all-zero columns by subtracting the
renormalizations the arithmetic decoder would have performed: while the
run-length context's MPS is a zero, each of those columns decodes one
zero and only A changes.

Pass the arithmetic state in from the caller so it stays in registers
across the passes.

Signed-off-by: Justin Jacob <159104807+Justin24506@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavcodec/jpeg2000dec.c | 486 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 378 insertions(+), 108 deletions(-)

